# Validate → commit → push (default)

When finishing implementation or cleanup in this repo, **always** run this loop unless the user explicitly says not to commit/push (e.g. plan-only, “don’t push”).

## 1. Validate (must pass before commit)

- `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` from `compose/` (or equivalent module build for touched code)
- Unit tests for changed packages (`:app:testDebugUnitTest --tests '…'`)
- Fix failures; re-run until green
- Do **not** commit known-broken builds

## 2. Commit

- Stage **source, tests, docs** relevant to the change
- Exclude build caches (`**/build/**`), secrets, and unrelated junk
- Follow repo commit style (concise why-focused message, HEREDOC `-m`)
- Do **not** wait for a separate “please commit” — finishing the task implies commit

## 3. Push

- `git push -u origin HEAD` (or `git push origin main` after a local merge)
- Do **not** wait for a separate “please push” — finishing the task implies push
- Still **never** force-push to `main`/`master` unless the user explicitly demands it

## Overrides

| User says | Behavior |
|-----------|----------|
| Plan mode / “don’t implement” | No commit/push |
| “Don’t commit” / “don’t push” | Skip that step only |
| “Commit only” | Validate + commit; skip push |
